#!/bin/bash
# repo2docker's CondaBuildPack starts every image from its own base
# environment, which already includes jupyterlab (and its jupyter-resource-usage
# extension) -- before environment.yml is even applied. `mamba env update`
# only adds/updates packages, it never removes ones already present, so
# simply omitting jupyterlab from environment.yml isn't enough: it's still
# in the final image, and its federated extensions expect newer core
# JupyterLab module versions than the pinned voila (see environment.yml)
# bundles, breaking ipywidgets rendering under Voila entirely. Explicitly
# remove it here, after the base+environment.yml install, so it's actually
# gone from the final image.
set -e
mamba remove -y jupyterlab jupyter-resource-usage 2>/dev/null || true

# There is also a separate, still-unresolved MathJax-related crash
# ("Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'Queue')" in voila's
# bundled JS) that keeps ipywidgets stuck at "Loading widget..." even with
# jupyterlab removed. A Voila.mathjax_url override (pointing at a no-op
# stub) fixed this when passed as a CLI flag in local testing, but the
# equivalent voila_config.py / VoilaConfiguration route did NOT take
# effect -- confirmed via browser console, the crash still occurred with
# the config file in place. Needs more investigation before shipping a fix
# here; not included yet.
